From 8c529a840e61defea98cfcbebc8eff49c27c7c74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anatoliy Klymenko <anatoliy.klymenko@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Oct 2025 14:30:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 179/190] drm: xlnx: mmi-dc: MMI DC planector interface

commit 58f8a00d41628a2c66753c6c21970b3f339bb5d6 from
https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx.git xlnx_rebase_v6.12

MMI DC supports multiple modes of operations: non-live (both planes are
driven by a DMA engine), live (one or two planes are driven by video
streams produced by external FPGA CRTCs), and mixed (a combination of live
and non-live modes). DRM framework doesn't support such complicated
pipelines out of the box. This dual DRM plane / bridge interface provides
a mean to connect MMI DC to an extarnal FPGA CRTC. Plane part allow to
compose and blend external video signal into MMI DC output video signal.
Bridge part provides virtual DRM connector interface to an upstream CRTC.

Signed-off-by: Anatoliy Klymenko <anatoliy.klymenko@amd.com>
Reviewed-by: Vishal Sagar <vishal.sagar@amd.com>
